==Equipment==
Ranged is the recommended attack style for Doom. The [[twisted bow]] is the strongest weapon to use, given Doom's Magic level of 275. The demonbane [[scorching bow]] is the next best alternative, as its damage only slightly trails behind the twisted bow and is far cheaper. The faster attack speed of the scorching bow is suboptimal: it generates 25% more acid, it's more difficult to attack at every opportunity while avoiding damage, and it misses an attack opportunity at the end of car phase (which does not last a multiple of 4 ticks).

Doom is technically weakest to melee crush attacks, but the fight has many mechanics that make melee unfriendly.

===Special attack weapons===
The [[Zaryte crossbow]] is the most powerful special attack weapon and should be paired with regular [[Ruby bolts (e)|enchanted ruby bolts]] for cost efficiency, as the [[Ruby dragon bolts (e)|dragon variant]] provides no additional benefit in this scenario. When to use it will vary - at delve levels 1-4, a successful special attack can help speed up the fight and reach deeper quicker. However, at delve levels 6+, it is not recommended to use the crossbow special attack as the opener due to the necessity of the [[#Rockblock|Rockblock]] strategy at higher delve levels. As such, it is recommended to use the crossbow special attack once the car phase starts to guarantee a high [[successful hit]] (as all attacks are 100% accurate in that form), or if health/supplies are low, preserve energy for a special attack that restores hitpoints or prayer on the [[volatile earth]] (ex. a [[toxic blowpipe]]) for a large amount of restoration.

For players without a Zaryte crossbow, their next best option is a [[crystal halberd]], which guarantees a minimum of 46 damage on each melee punish (two bonus hits of 23). The halberd matches the guaranteed damage from a [[Scythe of Vitur]] (three bonus hits of 15), has very useful bonus range and is much more available to players. Bringing extra switches for melee punish is not recommended, as the damage increase is marginal and inventory spots are very valuable.

[[Rosewood blowpipe]] special attacks are a viable budget alternative to [[Dragon knife]] special attacks, as its max hit is only 2 lower and it costs significantly less ({{Coins|{{GEP|Rune dart}}}} and {{Coins|{{GEP|Dragon knife}}}} per special respectively).

When car phase starts, use a Zaryte crossbow special or dump 3-4 dragon knife special attacks. At deeper delves, using short ranged weapons can be difficult without a roadblock setup. The goal is to deal enough damage to Doom so the player can skip its dangerous earthen shield phase (or at least kill Doom before it uses shockwaves).

A [[lightbearer]] is highly recommended over other rings, as special attacks are important on key phases of the fight. Upgraded [[Death Charge]] from [[Yama]] is also very strong, as Death Charge procs on both Doom and its larvae. With upgraded death charge and a lightbearer, players can restore 40-50% energy per level. Special attack energy does not restore between floors, and a floor completion will reset special attack energy restoration (i.e it will always take 30/15 seconds for the first special restore tick on the next floor).

Defense-draining weapons are not recommended. Doom has a defence reduction cap of 60, has guaranteed accuracy on several phases, and resets defence on each floor.

====Summary====
Best in slot:
* Bring a Zaryte crossbow, scythe, and crystal halberd.
* On 1-4, immediately crossbow spec. Use scythe for punishes.
* On 5-8+, do not immediately crossbow spec. Use the halberd spec on melee punish attacks.
* When car phase starts, crossbow spec as your first attack.

Budget:
* Bring a toxic blowpipe and a crystal halberd.
* On all phases, use halberd spec on melee punishes.
* Toxic blowpipe spec can restore the maximum health possible on volatile earth if deemed necessary.

===Masori vs Elite void===
The best primary ranged gear sets are  [[Elite Void Knight equipment]] or [[Masori armour|fortified masori]]. Both give a very similar performance, but there are various factors that can influence the gear used.

With a [[scorching bow]], elite void with [[seeking dragon arrow]]s is recommended. It has about the same DPS as Masori, and has higher damage on the 100% accuracy phases of doom. [[Elite void]] is also much cheaper and has very low reclaim costs, which minimises death costs and allows players to upgrade other slots.

With a [[twisted bow]], fortified masori is the strongest available armour. However, it's only marginally more effective than void and has much higher reclaim costs;  masori is not required and is only recommended to experienced delvers who are not expecting many deaths. 

===Spellbook choice===
If using the [[Eye of Ayak]], players may choose to use the [[Lunar spellbook]] for access to [[Cure Me]] with [[Spellbook Swap]] for [[Death Charge]], though keep in mind the Eye will not disrupt the Doom's shield phase charging and will increase death costs if not protected.

If not using the Eye of Ayak, players should stay on the [[Arceuus spellbook]] with runes for Death Charge. Thralls are not recommended, as their attacks cause Doom to spread much more acid.

