Melee Punish=
It's worth bringing a multi-hit melee weapon for the melee punish attack ([[Doom of Mokhaiotl/Strategies#Melee punish|discussed above]]). Devoting inventory slots to marginally improve a melee punish — such as melee strength gear, void melee helm or a super combat potion (neither of which even increases the bonus damage) — is not worthwhile. Halberds can avoid melee range (which requires a quick click off to avoid a melee attack) and give useful positional flexibility around acid.
{{Recommended equipment
| style = Melee punish
| 2h2 = {{plink|Noxious halberd}}{{efn|Noxious halberd's average hit is about half of that of the crystal halberd spec. It can be considered for deep delves to spawn less acid. It is also much easier to use without getting meleed by the boss due to its increased attack range, especially on deeper delves with more floor acid and less time to react to boulders.}}
| 2h3 = {{plink|Dual macuahuitl|txt=Dual macuahuitl}} or other multi-hit melee weapons
| 2h4 = {{plink|Darklight|txt=Darklight}} or its variants{{efn|While normally effective on demons, has a very low base strength bonus. Can be used in a pinch to interrupt the charge beam, but will miss out on significant amounts of free damage.|name=darklight}}
| special1 = {{plink|Crystal halberd}}{{efn|Special attack should be used as long as it will not interfere with a zcb spec.|name=spec}}
| special2 = {{plink|Dragon claws}}{{efn|Dragon claws paired with at least 25 strength bonus can beat Crystal halberd, but as a 4 tick attack it is much harder to use, especially while dodging mechanics.|name=claw}} / {{plink|Crimson kisten}}
}}
