==Plugins==
All of the following plugins are available on both officially approved third-party [[Game client]]s. On RuneLite they must be installed separately from the Plugin Hub, accessed from the Configuration button (wrench icon on sidebar), then clicking the Plugin Hub button (right-most plug icon). On HDOS these plugins come preinstalled.

===Better NPC Highlight===
* Check "Highlight Menu Names" at the bottom of the plugin settings
* For true tile highlighting, paste <code>14711:2,14713:1,14712:5,14788:2,14789:5,</code> to "Hull" or "True Tile" -> "True Tile IDs" for demonic larvae at delve level 4+, and giant demonic larvae at delve level 8+.
** For burrowed Doom and the [[earthen shield]]: paste <code>14709,14715:5,</code> in "True Tile IDs", on the end of the Larvae ID's (if included).
* To distinguish regular Doom and shielded doom: Add <code>*mokhaiotl:1, *mokhaiotl (shielded):5,</code> to "Tile" -> "Tile Names".
** Select the "Tile Highlight" tickbox to enable NPC highlighting and choose the colour and highlight settings preferred.

===Custom Menu Swaps===
* To have the [[demonic larvae]] attack options appear on top of anything else: Add <code>Attack,demonic*larva*</code> to "Custom Swaps"
** For waves 8+, add <code>Attack,giant demonic*larva*</code> to "Custom Swaps" for giant larvae

===Visual Metronome===
* Visual Metronome checked, 'Tick Count' set to 20
* Under Tick Number Settings, check 'Show Metronome Tick Number'
** To change the color of the number, edit the 'Tick Number Color' setting under Tick Number Settings
** To change the background, edit the color values under 'Color Settings'
* Set Hotkey Settings > Tick Cycle Reset Hotkey to any comfortable key, and Reset to Tick to 0
* Press the hotkey when the Volatile Earth spawns, the boss will begin the shockwave attack when the timer hits 20.

===Radius Markers===
Radius Markers (found in the sidebar after installation) can be used to outline specific attack ranges from the Doom, to enable safe drag attacks with a halberd. Copy the below import and then click the import icon, which will add a 4-width floor outline around Doom, and meleeing Doom with a halberd while on the inner edge of the line will always safely not drag you into melee distance. Additionally, this marker will change from blue to green when the Doom initiates their shield phase, so that you do not mistakenly attack with a halberd and cause a long attack delay.
